// parsing code in the editor (§4.4): the set inside the raw block reassembles it as a whole (the
// unit is the block itself, the test 230; the node stores the id), the result of parsing is a
// derivative, editing it invalidates:
// 
// The block text is as written.
// program: editor_raw.vish
open_view module
run
// expect: output text="16\n" ok=true
// 3 → 30: Next launch with new parsing
pointer 1 @{1 0 6
key 1 0
// expect: курсор:   print(sum_of() {1 2 30‸ x});
// expect-not: n_hole
run 
// expect: output text="43\n" ok=true
// a string instead of a number - the rule will make the atom a component, the error - when executed
key 1 Backspace
key 1 Backspace
key 1 "
key 1 a
key 1 "
// expect: print(sum_of() {1 2 "a" x});
run 
// expect: ok=false
// rule correction: the block is re-examined by the same text
pointer 1 @sum_parse:3 0 0
key 1 n
key 1 e
key 1 g
// expect: syntax {r} => negsum_parse(r);
run 
// expect: output text="7\n" ok=true
